{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Defect\n\n`docker_unaccounted_bytes` subtracts Docker-ledger apparent sizes from a Docker-root filesystem total measured as allocated blocks. Those units are not commensurable, so XFS allocation overhead appears as unreachable Docker residue. On 2026-09-05 the host measurement was:\n\n- allocated Docker root: 13,642,739,712 bytes\n- apparent Docker root: 12,140,814,875 bytes\n- Docker ledger: 10,957,600,000 bytes\n\nThe current calculation reports 2,685,139,712 bytes unaccounted. The commensurable apparent-size residue is 1,183,214,875 bytes. The sibling `docker_storage_bytes` metric must remain allocated-block based because it reports real disk consumption.\n\n## Design\n\nReplace the Docker-root filesystem census with one metadata pass that returns both sizes:\n\n- allocated bytes = sum of `st_blocks * 512`, preserving `docker_storage_bytes`;\n- apparent bytes = sum of `st_size`, used only as the minuend for `docker_unaccounted_bytes`;\n- overlay2 breadcrumb = accumulated allocated bytes for paths under the overlay2 subtree;\n- hardlinks are de-duplicated by device+inode so allocated/appparent totals retain `du`-like semantics;\n- the pass stays inside the Docker root filesystem (`find -xdev`) and keeps the existing overlay2 cross-device guard.\n\nThis avoids the rejected second `du` walk from bug 9313: one traversal emits all filesystem quantities, and `docker system df` is still called once for the Docker ledger and container rows. No threshold raise and no prune action are part of this fix.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1: `docker_storage_bytes` remains allocated-block based, while `docker_unaccounted_bytes` subtracts the Docker ledger from apparent Docker-root bytes.\n- [ ] AC2: a defect-seeded test replays allocated=13,642,739,712, apparent=12,140,814,875, ledger=10,957,600,000 and expects `docker_unaccounted_bytes=1,183,214,875`; the old allocated-minus-ledger value would fail.\n- [ ] AC3: the implementation obtains allocated and apparent Docker-root sizes from one filesystem traversal, not two `du` walks.\n- [ ] AC4: the alarm rationale records the measured baseline and corrects the old “hundreds of MB” assumption without raising the threshold.\n- [ ] AC5: the runbook guidance distinguishes allocation overhead from genuine unaccounted content and does not overstate container JSON logs/buildkit/image as the usual source.\n\n## Verification\n\nRun the targeted docker-storage observability tests, Terraform alarm/runbook tests touched by this change, `make lint`, and full `make verify` with the required `GIT_CONFIG_*` unsets before push."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788891372845423001,"uuid":"5a0e3dd2-a83c-4122-9d6b-47e91d419e66"}